## Center diagram in Visual by default and fix Graph ready status badge legibility

Context: In Mapping Studio's Visual tab, the diagram loaded at (0, 0) without
centering or fitting to the canvas. Also, the "Graph ready · Lakebase" (and
other backend) readiness badges rendered with low contrast and washed-out text/icons
because global `.badge.bg-success { background-color: #28a745 !important; }`
overrode the transparent background and paired with dark green text (`#198754`),
while the brand mark and backend label were washed out by `opacity-75`.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-design.js
   Implemented `centerMappingDiagram(animate)`: computes bounding box and
   centroid of mapping nodes, scales and translates them to fit centered within
   the visible container with comfortable padding. Called on initial map render,
   on tab switch to Visual (`MappingStudioTabs._onShown`), in `resizeMapSvg()`,
   on Reset Layout, and on the "Reset view" button click. Exposes
   `window.centerMappingDiagram`.
2. src/front/static/global/css/mapping.css
   Removed legacy forced `.badge.bg-success { background-color: #28a745 !important; }`
   and `.badge.bg-secondary` rules that broke Bootstrap subtle/opacity styling.
3. src/front/static/query/js/query-sync.js
   Updated `updateKgReadyIndicators()` to use `bg-success-subtle text-success-emphasis border border-success-subtle fw-medium`,
   removed `opacity-75` from the backend label/icon, and updated related readiness badges
   for consistent legibility.
4. src/front/static/query/css/query-sync.css & src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   Added clear flex-aligned `.kg-status-indicator .badge` sizing and `.ob-brand-icon`
   dimensions across all subpages.
5. src/front/static/domain/js/domain-validation.js
   Updated existence and status badges to use subtle high-contrast styling.
6. tests/units/front/test_mapping_studio_tabs.py
   Added contract tests for `centerMappingDiagram` and Visual centering integration.
7. tests/units/front/test_kg_readiness_indicator.py
   Added contract assertions for subtle high-contrast readiness badge classes and visible backend brand mark.

